From: Christopher Owen <root@your.mom>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 14:13:58 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Vectorize sampler casts and use pitched DMA for large FP32
 copies

Upstream base: 486d01e07cf3ba37296a78a8a0cf8da26cf19295. Rationale: eliminate the scalar-copy slowdown while preserving small-batch parallelism. Quality: owned bit-exact FP32 outputs, unchanged source/RNG, explicit CUDA errors and native current-stream ordering. Tests: common candidate passes 1,167 checks twice; selected DMA screen passes twice; final sampler gate and new graph/side-stream cases pending. Upstream status: local experiment, not submitted.
